# verbs.pdl - the rmmc manifest: which verbs are EVENT PAGES (BOOK 16.game/EVENT-VERB-PAGES-DESIGN.md; same grammar as @.apps/tearit-map/verbs.pdl). Read by &.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/verbgen.+x
#   verbgen check @.apps/rmmc   engine source <-> this file <-> events/ must agree
#   verbgen gen   @.apps/rmmc   write events/<verb>/ for every page=yes verb (never overwrites an edited package)
# The rules are ONE op (vox_op, D105/D137: the append-only vox ledger is the only authority); a page runs rmmc_verb, which calls vox_op and then rmmc_project_op (the projection the engine draws).
# Who may call: the key driver (rmmc_driver, a human) and the beat op (rmmc_beat_op, a harness or an AI) both play these pages; the seat row says which of them may write.
GAME | rmmc | rmmc_verb | ops/+x/rmmc_verb.+x | ops/rmmc_verb.c
#   VERB | name | page | trigger | args | what it does
VERB | spawn | yes | ui | x z | Asa appears on the island column (x, row z) at the top of its ground (refused 11 over sky or off the map, 18 when she is already on the island)
VERB | walk  | yes | ui | dir | one column n, e, s or w; the height is resolved from the heightmap (a step up of 1, 2 out of water, a drop of 3, shallow water only; refused 11 off the island, 18 for a wall, a cliff or deep water)
VERB | face  | yes | ui | dir | turn on the spot (a FACE row: the facing is a fold of the ledger)
VERB | jump  | yes | ui |     | hop up one level and land back on the same column (both MOVE rows or none; 15 with no ground under the feet)
VERB | reset | yes | ui |     | back to the spawn point (a RESET row)
VERB | seat  | yes | ui | who | who drives Asa: human or harness (a SEAT row; the last row wins; no row = harness)
# mine and place act on the column IN FRONT of Asa (her facing); place uses the hotbar pick (play/pick.txt, default dirt). pick is not a verb: it is a preference written by rmmc_pick_op.
# Only the top block of a column can be mined or built on (overhangs and tunnels are not representable, plan 7).
VERB | mine  | yes | ui |     | dig the top block of the column in front (a MINE row; the column drops one level; refused 13 with nothing to dig, 11 off the island)
VERB | place | yes | ui |     | put the picked block on top of the column in front (a PLACE row; the column rises one level; refused 11 off the island)
